WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.360
You've found a sweater
pattern that you love.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:11.010
The neckline, design, and stitch pattern
are just perfect, but it's sleeveless.

3
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.080
Now, I don't know about you,

4
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:17.300
but I'm past the point of wanting
to show off my arms and I need sleeves.

5
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.100
If the pattern is a drop shoulder or basic

6
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:26.980
square armhole, you can easily add sleeves
with the Knit It Now custom sleeves tool.

7
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:33.300
Measure both your front and back armholes
from the pattern diagram or instructions.

8
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.300
Determine your desired sleeve length,
short sleeve, three quarter or full

9
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:47.680
length, and be sure to adjust the wrist
or arm measurement accordingly.

10
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.600
Choosing your custom sleeve pattern
instructions, choose to pick up and knit

11
00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:00.380
the sleeves from the top down
or start at the cuff and knit up.

12
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.460
No more bare arms.

13
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.640
Make the sweater your own.

